window.docContents[150].resolve({"/Calculational-proofs/#Kernel-Hom___-Tactics-for-Kernel-Categorical-Reasoning--Calculational-proofs--String-diagrams-of-the-calculation--First-calculation":{"contents":"Step 1. Marginalization of the right-hand side of the sufficiency equation.\n\n\n\nStep 2. By sufficiency.\n\n\n\nStep 3. Since s is a Markov kernel, discarding its output is discarding its input, and the copy disappears by its counit law.\n\n\n\nStep 4. By ancillarity.\n\n\n\nStep 5. Since s ∘ₖ p is a Markov kernel, discarding its output is discarding its input.\n\n\n\n","context":"Kernel-Hom: Tactics for Kernel Categorical Reasoning\u0009Calculational proofs\u0009String diagrams of the calculation","header":"2.2.1. First calculation","id":"/Calculational-proofs/#Kernel-Hom___-Tactics-for-Kernel-Categorical-Reasoning--Calculational-proofs--String-diagrams-of-the-calculation--First-calculation"}});